      "role": "user",
      "content": "<|channel>thought\n<channel|><|channel>thought\n<channel|><|channel>thought\n<channel|><|channel>thought\n<channel|>Wait, 30 days' notice? That sounds like they can just tell us the price is going up and we have to deal with it. I thought we were looking for a contract where we have the final say on any price hikes. \n\nDoes Section 4.2 specifically allow them to increase the rates unilaterally (meaning they just decide and notify us), or is there a requirement for us to sign off on the change first? I need to be 100% sure before I send this to the CFO.",
